# Create a Supabase project, then enable Authentication → Providers:
#   Google
#
# Redirect URLs (Authentication → URL Configuration). List both, or a
# rejected localhost callback is replaced with Site URL (production):
#   http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#   http://127.0.0.1:3000/auth/callback
#   https://nfinit.vercel.app/auth/callback
#
# Site URL can stay the production origin. It is only the fallback.
#
# Copy these into Vercel and frontend/.env.local:
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key
#
# After applying supabase/migrations, create the backend's own login role
# (never connect as postgres; see deploy/railway.env.example), then copy these
# into Railway and remove NFNIT_ALLOW_LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS:
# NFNIT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://nfinit_api.PROJECT:PASSWORD@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=only-for-legacy-hs256-projects
